                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "059688c0-0507-36dd-a925-0194e5efaeb6",
                        "entry_id": "7576ae14-4cbf-34b6-9ba2-6aefc6fc890a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "орнитол. птица из отряда аистообразных, единственный представитель семейства китоглавых"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35ea0895-c1a8-49da-9bc5-2f507c1d5bd6",
                                "sense_id": "059688c0-0507-36dd-a925-0194e5efaeb6",
                                "text": "Китоглавы живут в обширных болотах, особенно по бассейну Белого Нила; держатся в одиночку или небольшими обществами среди зарослей папируса и камыша; питаются рыбой, которую ловят, как цапли."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "97b94da9-fae2-4bdc-8273-9f65b38fc54c",
                        "source_entry_id": "7576ae14-4cbf-34b6-9ba2-6aefc6fc890a",
                        "source_sense_id": "059688c0-0507-36dd-a925-0194e5efaeb6",
                        "target_lang_word": "shoebill",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shoebill",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                        "entry_id": "f8c46393-50b9-37a4-b7b4-08ac6e7d79ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Balaeniceps rex, a tall wading bird related to the stork, native to tropical African swamps; the sole species of the family Balaenicipitidae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "791e51b3-7b02-40c1-9b7d-f63130774fec",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "The Shoebill is distinctive in many aspects of its biology, and is thus, we feel, most appropriately placed in its own family, the Balaenicipitidae (L. Buxton et al. 1978, Kahl 1979a). The fact that we have included it in this book, while excluding the Hamerkop, indicates that we believe the Shoebill to be closer to the storks (Kahl 1967b, 1979c); however the jury remains out as to how close."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a48c2550-9e23-49d7-ab3c-f65608ff08bb",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, Birdlife International recently classified it as near-globally threatened, and it is classed as CITES Appendix 2, which means that trade in shoebills, or their capture for any harmful activity, is forbidden by international law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fabf0ed4-f72a-4cd9-8c0f-e9bfca41ec57",
                                                "sense_id": "740dee32-7165-3dd6-9c6f-698752ea4321",
                                                "text": "The monstrous and awesome shoebill is possibly the most bizarre bird on the African continent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "942dbc49-cc46-4614-8ba1-0c1775daf2f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "7576ae14-4cbf-34b6-9ba2-6aefc6fc890a",
                        "source_sense_id": "059688c0-0507-36dd-a925-0194e5efaeb6",
                        "target_lang_word": "whalehead",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whalehead",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "696b92be-eac8-33e5-a551-7b3fdbfb2b19",
                                        "entry_id": "920f1541-0f6e-3f7e-b03f-b5f1e93d2958",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of shoebill (wading bird)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6e39903-3a86-4427-ab91-3e6b2c50ff50",
                                                "sense_id": "696b92be-eac8-33e5-a551-7b3fdbfb2b19",
                                                "text": "The shoebill, whalehead or boatbill, as it is sometimes called, is one of Africa's strangest and rarest endemics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed26597a-658d-3edb-90f9-881e3d861a5c",
                                        "entry_id": "920f1541-0f6e-3f7e-b03f-b5f1e93d2958",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of sand dune in North Carolina."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57964a4a-6701-4290-ba68-22037046c0cd",
                                                "sense_id": "ed26597a-658d-3edb-90f9-881e3d861a5c",
                                                "text": "The strong north winds pile the sands up into great barchannes or medanoes, crescentic sand dunes known locally as whaleheads, which are moving steadily southward."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "336b9054-0dbe-47f5-add9-16c5ab16028d",
                                                "sense_id": "ed26597a-658d-3edb-90f9-881e3d861a5c",
                                                "text": "Huge dunes, called “whaleheads” by locals, developed on Hatteras during this time and swept across the island."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa09b5cf-f82e-4661-991c-c7119e5dc2a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "7576ae14-4cbf-34b6-9ba2-6aefc6fc890a",
                        "source_sense_id": "059688c0-0507-36dd-a925-0194e5efaeb6",
